Subject: [PATCH] stop the child-exit handler before releasing its process table

Shutdown kills the scanner and HTTP children, then frees the children table
while SIGCHLD still invokes process_handle_child_termination(). A late
child exit can therefore make remove_process_info() read freed memory.

Ignore SIGCHLD before terminating the remaining children and releasing the
table. Do this after monitor_stop(), which uses SIGCHLD to wake its inotify
thread and joins that thread. The handler can then no longer run while the
table is freed, and exiting children are reaped automatically.

--- a/minidlna.c
+++ b/minidlna.c
@@ -1360,6 +1360,10 @@ shutdown:
 #endif
 
 	/* kill other child processes */
+	/* The monitor uses SIGCHLD to wake its thread. After it has joined,
+	 * prevent late child exits from accessing the freed process table.
+	 */
+	signal(SIGCHLD, SIG_IGN);
 	process_reap_children();
 	free(children);
 
